; A comma whose meaning the digits cannot settle ("1,075") is read by
; what the commodity has learned so far, so the EUR and GBP orders below
; give values 1000x apart.  This file pins that order dependence for
; commodities with no established decimal style, and the cases that
; must keep parsing as they do: a period that confirms a decimal comma
; (even after a decimal period), a declared format, and a precision
; learned only from a price directive.  A guessed decimal comma on a
; commodity already written with a decimal period is an error: see
; decimal-comma-conflict.test.

; EUR: the thousands reading comes first, so "1,075 EUR" is 1075 and
; "0,075 EUR" then teaches EUR the decimal comma.
2024/01/01 EUR thousands first
    EUR    1,075 EUR
    Equity

2024/01/02 EUR zero integer part second
    EUR    0,075 EUR
    Equity

; GBP: the same two amounts in the other order; "0,075 GBP" teaches the
; decimal comma first, so "1,075 GBP" is 1.075.
2024/01/03 GBP zero integer part first
    GBP    0,075 GBP
    Equity

2024/01/04 GBP thousands second
    GBP    1,075 GBP
    Equity

; CHF: a period before the comma confirms the decimal comma, so a
; commodity first seen with a thousands comma still accepts it.
2024/01/05 CHF thousands comma
    CHF    1,000 CHF
    Equity

2024/01/06 CHF period confirms decimal comma
    CHF    1.000,50 CHF
    Equity

; CAD: a commodity already written with a decimal period still accepts
; a comma that a period confirms; only a guessed comma is an error.
2024/01/07 CAD decimal period
    CAD    1,000.50 CAD
    Equity

2024/01/08 CAD period confirms decimal comma
    CAD    1.000,50 CAD
    Equity

; NOK: a declared format never migrates, so the heuristic stays local to
; the number and "0,07 NOK" is 0.07.
commodity NOK
    format 1,000.00 NOK

2024/01/09 NOK declared period style
    NOK    0,07 NOK
    Equity

; SEK: a precision learned only from a price directive does not
; establish a decimal period.
P 2024/01/10 XAU 1.10 SEK

2024/01/11 SEK precision from a price only
    SEK    0,075 SEK
    Equity

test bal --flat --no-total CAD CHF EUR GBP NOK SEK
        2.001,00 CAD  CAD
        2.000,50 CHF  CHF
       1.075,075 EUR  EUR
           1,150 GBP  GBP
            0.07 NOK  NOK
           0,075 SEK  SEK
end test
